# On-screen keyboard. xvkbd rather than onboard: onboard manages its own
# window and refuses window-manager decoration, so it could not be dragged,
# and its auto-show needs the application to publish focused text fields
# over accessibility, which Carbide Motion does not do. This one is a plain
# X window the window manager can place, raise and decorate like any other.
xvkbd

# A single launcher button so the keyboard can be brought back after it is
# dismissed. Not used as a taskbar; the machine runs one application.
tint2
adwaita-icon-theme

# Screensaver. phosphor is a plain text renderer with no GL, which is both
# cheaper than the graphical hacks and more useful: it shows the share address.
xscreensaver
xscreensaver-data
